    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Discusses the fact that we live in a super-sized world in which our perception of what is an appropriate serving of food is distorted. Increases awareness of portion sizes by examining questions such as how psychology and tricks of perception influence how much people eat, how food labels can mislead about calories, and why getting more food for the same money is not always a true value. Provides advice on estimating serving sizes.</marc:subfield>
